# id sfr sfr_IR sfr_UV L_IR L_UV flag z z_type f24tot ef24tot L_1600 L_2800 beta
# 7/16/2014 by K.E. Whitaker
#
# Adopts the photometric redshift (z_type=2), or spectroscopic redshift (z_type=1) where available.
# We use a luminosity-independent conversion from the total 24 micron flux density to the 
# bolometric IR luminosity (L_IR), which is the log average of the Dale & Helou (2002) templates.
# Total SFR = 1.09x10^-10(L_IR+2.2*L_UV)  (assuming a Chabrier IMF and the Bell+05 UV conversion)
# where L_UV = 1.5*L2800.  Beta is the UV continuum slope.  When flag=1, this signifies
# 24 micron aperture flux densities with S/N ratio between 0 and 1, whereas flag=2 signifies
# negative 24 micron aperture flux densities, and flag=-99 when z<=0.
#
